      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "Eric Jones",
      "description": "Blasting at the Penrhyn Quarry viewed from Cwm Ffrydlas I had just started on my lunch when the 'take cover' siren was sounded at the Penrhyn. This was followed a minute or two later by a series of blasts and shortly afterwards by the warble of the 'all clear'. Today's firings are a tame affair compared with those of yesteryear when there would be simultaneous blasting on all the galleries, but it was enough to bring back memories of a time when you could set your watch by the twice daily blastings - always on the hour - from different quarries in the district.",
